# Amendment 1.0.4: split strict P01 capture admission from comparison

C09 owns isolated differential runtime qualification, including actual native/Rust execution, source and file admission, resource ownership and teardown. A selected P01 comparison is one development prerequisite within that scope. The repaired prototype `/workspace/build/builderbob/syson-batch22-20261029/compare_p01.py`, SHA-256 `56e59184a7190cc6beffc7f5e413e4fbff9ff9b965f02740b976accce931ec5f`, is 686 lines of frozen, unexecuted preparation. It exceeds the ordinary production review budget. This amendment assigns two modules before partitioning or execution; it does not grant a budget exception or qualify the prototype.

## Assign every frozen behavior before coding

C09a owns `porting/rust-parity-evidence/C09/batch22-comment-comparison/capture_p01.py`, its separate `tests/test_capture_p01.py` and `porting/rust-parity-evidence/C09a/`. It implements strict capture/schema/corpus/provenance and qualification-receipt admission. The frozen source assignment is lines 1–324, 474–480 and 483–485: 334 retained lines plus the initial factoring estimate of approximately 340 changed production lines. The authored estimate is at most 650, including focused typed controls; actual additions and deletions after ordinary formatting control execution admission.

C09b follows landed C09a and owns `compare_p01.py`, its separate `tests/test_compare_p01.py` and `porting/rust-parity-evidence/C09b/`. It preserves native/Rust projections, exact error classification, comparison/reporting and the CLI. Its assigned projection/CLI ranges are 325–473, 481–482, 486–527 and 655–686: 225 retained lines. It also retains all 35 composed controls in lines 528–654, a 127-line region. The three assignments cover all 686 frozen source lines exactly once. Retaining provenance is not permission to discard a behavior while moving code.

Count the 127 control lines conservatively as implementation when they remain CLI-adjacent: 225 + 127 = 352 before module binding and factoring. C09b's upper production estimate is 390 and its authored estimate is 700. Both children keep the hard caps of 400 changed handwritten production and 900 authored lines. All validators, helper functions, imports, CLI code and coordinator wiring count; placing them under an evidence directory grants no discount. Meaningful tests also count toward authored lines. If actual formatted counts exceed either cap, adopt another meaningful split before execution. Do not compress code, delete tests or extend an unrelated observer exception.

The root coordinator owns the shared README. Each author owns only its module, separate tests and evidence path; module imports belong to that module's production count. Before C09b executes its sibling, it must bind and verify the exact landed capture-module bytes and API. Preserve the existing constructor validator's source-before-execution check. No unchecked import or cached-bytecode substitution can replace those bindings.

## Preserve source epochs, schemas and meaningful controls

Keep both complete P01 corpus epochs. The 15-case raw SHA-256 is `971dcf43457b511ee7f7df99b676c38179a6450b3241caf66d7a9682320982ca`; its canonical SHA-256 is `d4212968de38e574f8aebe8f5c64b9245115a36f057a7e5d46c8654702d0e348`. The 25-case raw SHA-256 is `c5fce29e6ac91d6d0c65ad657edfb12f20fe7bdc5a408ca3deaef6816a714cc6`; its canonical SHA-256 is `17d3985d0f5b64430715bda98c4ce8b211db22c916a52184b14b736232b0adb2`. Retain every case ID, order, source and origin field. Coherently truncating or reordering corpus and captures must still fail admission.

Keep the complete native bundle/prefix/embedded-module and source pins, the kernel pin, raw property descriptors, object/CST links, diagnostics, references and unavailable-accessor state. The existing public Rust constructor validator at `porting/rust-parity-evidence/C09/batch21-constructor-tools/compare_construction.py` remains an exact source input, SHA-256 `3d7d2451ff2300510cda71ad6c5debee6fab47193277d8c1292f2490eb7874d6`. Verify its bytes before compiling or executing them. C09a must exercise that real public schema validator rather than a permissive mirror.

C09a adds focused public-admission tests for malformed/overflowing JSON numbers, duplicate or missing keys/IDs, invalid descriptor flags, dangling object/CST links, incorrect byte/UTF-16 spans, source/epoch/provenance drift and receipt input/kernel/argv/exit/timeout mismatches. A changed validator module must be refused before its code executes. These focused tests supplement the original composed controls; they do not replace them.

C09b retains all 35 named controls, including native/Rust type, name and root changes; malformed or missing node/Datum/CST data; dropped nonselected `TypeReference`/`FeatureTyping`; ownership and source-location errors; raw reference text/spans; coherent corpus changes; false provenance; a misleading comment-interior refusal; truncated errors; missing native reference information; three receipt controls; and constructor-source binding. The machine policy records the exact list and original 127-line region hash. Normal and optimized Python runs must retain explicit behavioral guards. Preserve old silent-pass counterexamples, original tool versions and failed attempts as their own evidence; do not relabel old captures after a repair.

## Keep differences and evidence limits explicit

The comparison covers the complete captured AST type census, selected ordered names/node origins, finite ownership/reachability and raw reference text/source spans. Actual native objects supply expectations. Exact case-qualified semantic-comment/multiline-note restrictions and known recovered-input refusals remain explicit OPEN dispositions. Arbitrary text containing a comment marker cannot justify an unexpected Rust refusal. Malformed capture/schema/source/receipt input exits 2; real comparison differences exit 1. Missing native information remains visible rather than becoming a guessed value or a passing comparison.

The receipt proves only the input-map and command declarations it actually contains. Its retained limitation is: “Receipt input/command declarations are checked. The receipt has no output digest; capture-to-execution causality requires independent artifact/stdout review.” Hash-valid declarations cannot substitute for inspecting the actual captured stdout/artifacts and the process that produced them. Full fields/caches, resolved reference targets/getters, lifecycle, deployed native artifact correspondence, importer and UI behavior remain outside the selected comparison claim.

## Preserve C09, RR15 and the execution gates

C09 keeps its original source paths, tasks, C01/C02 source dependencies and normalized RR15 implementation dependency and accepted child. It additionally consumes C09b for implementation and requires both new children for acceptance. Its B05/B28/B32/B34 joint inputs, original 608-unit expanded implementation closure and complete original accepted-stage obligations remain. The policy reconstructs and hashes both the raw and normalized original parent, including the RR15 and joint-closure obligations.

The selected tools may prepare and qualify their existing pinned fixture interfaces independently of the unfinished application. Their source chain is C09a → C09b. This does not discharge C01/C02/RR15, expand the finite tool into general untrusted filesystem admission, or qualify actual native/Rust/database runtime lifecycle. Full file/resource admission, exact owned PID/start/port identities, readiness, timeout, cancellation, failure retention and teardown remain parent requirements. Native/UI workflows and meaningful screenshots, focus/accessibility, source/artifact correspondence and performance evidence remain required where applicable.

Runtime execution remains serialized under the coordinator, against reviewed owned synthetic inputs. The amendment grants no implementation, process or runtime lease and releases no held scope. Preserve workload-specific performance ranges, raw measurements and the rule that p95 requires at least 30 samples with a declared estimator. A selected comparison or seven-sample range does not establish UI usability, native capacity or production-language closure.

The contract becomes `SYSON-RUST-COMPLETION/1.0.4`, with 784 review units: all prior 782 plus C09a/C09b. All 55 historical implementation objects, prior integration history, original evidence, RR08/U10 policies and earlier amendments remain unchanged. Earlier named F10/F11 dispositions and C03a/C03b assignments retain their narrow scope; none grants these children a helper, observer or evidence-path exemption. Static refusal controls cover missing children, coherently removed dependency/readiness edges, weakened RR15/parent gates, widened scopes/caps, source/epoch changes and dropped controls. They establish planning integrity only; runtime evidence, RR16b/RR17 enforcement and independent acceptance review remain required.
